<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <meta name="description" content="Annotated box model practical by Shubhanshu Kushwaha.">
  <title>Box Model – Annotated</title>

  <style>
    body {
      font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
      max-width: 860px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 1.5rem;
      line-height: 1.5;
    }

    .student-details {
      background: #f1f5f9;
      border-left: 4px solid #1d3557;
      padding: 12px 16px;
      margin-bottom: 24px;
    }

    .my-box {
      width: 200px;
      height: 80px;
      padding: 20px;
      border: 10px solid #1d3557;
      margin: 30px;
      background: #a8dadc;
      display: grid;
      place-items: center;
      font-weight: bold;
    }

    .layer {
      display: grid;
      place-items: center;
      position: relative;
      text-align: center;
      font-size: .8rem;
    }

    .l-margin {
      background: #f9cb9c;
      padding: 36px;
    }

    .l-border {
      background: #ffe599;
      padding: 22px;
    }

    .l-padding {
      background: #b6d7a8;
      padding: 36px;
    }

    .l-content {
      background: #9fc5e8;
      padding: 28px 40px;
    }

    .tag {
      position: absolute;
      top: 3px;
      left: 8px;
      font-weight: bold;
    }

    .demo {
      display: flex;
      gap: 2rem;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      align-items: flex-start;
    }

    table {
      border-collapse: collapse;
    }

    th,
    td {
      border: 1px solid #999;
      padding: .35rem .7rem;
    }

    code {
      background: #eee;
      padding: 0 .25rem;
    }
  </style>
</head>

<body>

  <h1>Box Model of <code>.my-box</code></h1>

  <div class="student-details">
    <p><strong>Name:</strong> Shubhanshu Kushwaha</p>
    <p><strong>Student ID:</strong> BCAI2026081</p>
    <p><strong>Course:</strong> BCA</p>
    <p><strong>Mobile:</strong> 8887955490</p>
  </div>

  <div class="demo">
    <div class="my-box">Hello</div>

    <!-- Annotated diagram -->
    <div class="layer l-margin">
      <span class="tag">margin 30px</span>
      <div class="layer l-border">
        <span class="tag">border 10px</span>
        <div class="layer l-padding">
          <span class="tag">padding 20px</span>
          <div class="layer l-content">
            content<br>200 × 80
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Calculation (default <code>box-sizing: content-box</code>)</h2>

  <table>
    <tr>
      <th>Total width</th>
      <td>200 + (20×2) + (10×2) = <strong>260px</strong> (+60px margin = 320px of horizontal space)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th>Total height</th>
      <td>80 + (20×2) + (10×2) = <strong>140px</strong> (+60px margin = 200px)</td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <h2>With <code>box-sizing: border-box</code></h2>

  <p>
    The same <code>width: 200px</code> would already include padding and border,
    so the box would stay 200px wide and the content shrinks to 140px.
    That's why most developers add
    <code>* { box-sizing: border-box; }</code>.
  </p>

  <p>
    <em>
      Tip: Open DevTools (F12) → Elements → Computed tab to see this exact
      diagram for any element; screenshot it for your submission.
    </em>
  </p>

  <footer>
    <p>&copy; 2026 Shubhanshu Kushwaha | BCA</p>
  </footer>

</body>
</html>